Brittanie: Thank you. I didn't think that was the right.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.000
Brittanie: I hate your phone back.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:58.000
Brittanie: Perfect. Oh, perfect. Perfect.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Whitney Hodges: But when you're paying for traffic, we want to have the highest likelihood possible of getting that paid traffic to inquire with you. And so the way that we do that is by giving them one clear next step to take. A landing page, right?

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Basically asking them to inquire and to schedule a tour, right?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Whitney Hodges: So, it typically will take all the best pieces of your website and turn that into a long-form page with repeated and consistent calls to action with, like, buttons to get people to actually inquire.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.000
Brittanie: You'll see.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Brittanie: Thank you.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Whitney Hodges: And to enter your funnel. So, we do that through, um…

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Whitney Hodges: search campaigns on Google, because we want you to be showing up at the top of the search results for the people who are interested, right, in a day.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.000
Brittanie: Mm-hmm.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Brittanie: Mm-hmm.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:15:02.000
Whitney Hodges: in your location. And so, it's a similar sort of… well, it's a complement, right, to your, like, your organic SEO, like, that you're doing with Sarah, right? The goal there is to get you to the top of the results.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Brittanie: like, okay, I see other things going with. Yeah. Check.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:18.000
Whitney Hodges: On the organic side, that happens through what's on your website and blogging and things like that. But on the paid side, it's more of a matter of just setting up a campaign that's targeting the people that you want to target and the locations that you want to target with the keywords that you want to show up for.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.000
Brittanie: Yes, ma'am.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:33.000
Whitney Hodges: And what's nice about the paid side, too, is that we do have control over exactly what the headlines are saying, exactly what the ad text is saying, right? Whereas on the organic side, it's just kind of pulling from what it already sees on your website, and, like, Google.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.000
Brittanie: Mm-hmm.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Whitney Hodges: I think how that looks on the paid side, we really get to control what that is. You'll be showing up in the search results, most likely in both spots, an organic listing and a paid listing.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Whitney Hodges: You can tell the difference between the two, because the paid listings are typically gonna have that, like, sponsored tag.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Brittanie: It's not good. It's good.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Brittanie: Yeah.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, but we love it, you know, with client… when clients have strong SEO, and they're doing paid on… it's giving you double that visibility, double that…

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:00.000
Brittanie: But we love it.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Right? Like, in all likelihood, you're showing up twice when people are searching. They're seeing the ILIA's paid result, and they're seeing the organic result, which can really set you apart.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.000
Whitney Hodges: but.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:34.000
Whitney Hodges: So that was what happens on the Google ad side. But then, on the Meta ad side, the strategy is to set up what we like to call a full funnel of ads. So it's not just like one ad running a variety of different.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Brittanie: This is.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.000
Brittanie: Mm-hmm.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:59.000
Whitney Hodges: creatives, all with different objectives. So, at the top of the funnel, to completely cold audiences, we want to build that brand awareness. We want to really edit people because these ads are meant to be shown to people who have never heard of you before. They've never visited your website. They've never, you know, engaged with you on social media. So, we just want to get more eyeballs on your venue.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.000
Brittanie: Oh, wow.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.000
Brittanie: Let's see, it's more than that. It's just.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.000
Brittanie: Ah, okay.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Brittanie: Fantastic.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.000
Brittanie: Next slide.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Brittanie: Thank you. Mm-hmm.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Every day, systematically, right? Then the majority of the Meta Ads budget is going to go towards conversion campaigns. So, again, those would be ads that point people to the landing page with the goal of getting them to inquire, getting them to enter your funnel.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:33.000
Whitney Hodges: And then we also run bottom-of-funnel retargeting ads. So those are gonna be ads that specifically go to people who have visited the website before, who are… who have been on social media before, maybe they've seen an ad before, right? They're already somewhat familiar with the…

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.000
Brittanie: Okay.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.000
